name warning
category Package
revision 66616
shortdesc Global warnings at the end of the logfile
relocated 1
longdesc This package is obsolete. For LaTeX-format 2020-10-01 and
longdesc newer: Instead of \addglobalwarning{ something } use
longdesc \AddToHook{enddocument/info}{ something } and do not load the
longdesc warning package. For older formats this package provides a
longdesc command that generates a list of warnings that are printed out
longdesc at the very end of the logfile. This is useful for warnings
longdesc such as 'Rerun for this or that reason' or 'This is a draft,
longdesc change it before the final run'.
runfiles size=1
 RELOC/tex/latex/warning/warning.sty
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/warning
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics comp-supp
catalogue-version 0.10
